{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "metadata": {
  "note": "Nashville's only passenger train. The Music City Star opened on 18 September 2006 over former Tennessee Central Railway track between Lebanon and downtown Nashville, and was renamed the WeGo Star in 2019 when the Regional Transportation Authority of Middle Tennessee rebranded. It is a weekday commuter operation of a handful of round trips, sharing a freight line with the Nashville and Eastern Railroad.",
  "sources": [
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WeGo_Star (2006 opening, the Lebanon–Nashville route over the former Tennessee Central, and the 2019 renaming)",
   "OpenStreetMap route relations, extracted 29 August 2026; traced length is compared with the documented route length on each feature."
  ],
  "not_yet_sourced": "Headway and speed are estimates; no timetable was consulted, and the number of daily round trips has changed several times since 2006. The 2019 change from Music City Star to WeGo Star is treated as a rename of one operator, not an ownership change, so the feature is not split — that has not been verified against a source."
 },
